o=A.dW(a9,B.m,"Room 204 keeps losing Wi-Fi. It goes out for about a minute, comes back, and then does it again \u2014 maybe four or five times an hour. All of the Chromebooks in the room do it at the same time. Room 206 next door is fine. This started Tuesday and it is making the online practice tests impossible to finish.",B.lu,a,!1,B.cu,!0,"7:40 AM",B.m)
n=A.a([A.dW(a0,B.m,"Hi Dana \u2014 I swapped the access point in 204 this morning with a known-good unit. Please let me know tomorrow whether the drops continue.",B.lu,b0,!1,B.dg,!1,"1:15 PM",B.pC),A.dW(a9,B.m,"Still dropping this morning, twice already before 8. Same as before.",B.lu,a,!1,B.cu,!1,"8:02 AM",B.m),A.dW(a0,B.m,"New AP didn't change anything, so it isn't the radio. 204 shares an uplink with the library, which was re-cabled over the summer. I've opened a case with the vendor for the controller logs \u2014 case 88-41207.",B.m,a,!1,B.aV,!1,"8:31 AM",B.m),A.dW(a0,B.m,"Thanks for confirming. I've escalated this to our network vendor and I'm waiting on their logs. While we wait, please run the practice tests in the library \u2014 I've reserved it for your two afternoon blocks.",B.lu,a,!1,B.dg,!1,"9:05 AM",B.pC)],c3)
o=A.kk("Chase the vendor for the controller logs, and in the meantime move Room 204 off the shared channel.","Generated from 5 messages \xb7 9:10 AM","Every device in Room 204 loses Wi-Fi for about a minute at a time, several times an hour, and has done since Tuesday. Neighbouring rooms are unaffected. The access point was swapped on Wednesday and the behaviour continued, which points at the uplink or the channel rather than the AP itself. Waiting on the vendor's log export before the next step.",!0,A.a([$.b8r()],c5),"Network","Aug 21, 2026 \xb7 7:40 AM",p,c4,"Today \xb7 12:00 PM",a7,B.a3f,B.d6,"Building",B.a2E,a1,n,"TIX-39990",o,!0,a0,B.a2_,B.mz,0,"1h 48m over",B.I1,B.cH,"Wi-Fi dropping in Room 204",B.a3P,B.Yh,a8,B.pD,B.h8,a4,"3h","Wi-Fi Access","Aug 21, 2026 \xb7 9:05 AM",B.Zl)
